  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus disintegrates into two smaller parts, which have their velocities in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. The ratio of their nuclear sizes will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>.&nbsp;The value of &lsquo;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&rsquo; is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a579896b-2a60-4d04-b66c-20c8b04068f9-9894796.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 73px;\" /></p><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Using conservation of&nbsp;momentum during disintegration, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>We have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mtext>nuclear&#160;mass&#160;density</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>constant</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>",
